gametitle=Ghost in the Shell - Stand Alone Complex (NTSC-U) SLUS-21006 95CC86EF

[No-Interlacing]
author=heavyjam
description=Outputs a progressive frame instead of an interlaced one, with the DISPLAY origin corrected to match. The game already draws a full 640x448 frame from a fixed draw offset, so nothing is resampled and the picture does not move: at default settings the rendered frames are byte-identical to stock, and they stay identical with Screen Offsets enabled. What changes is that the frame is no longer flagged as interlaced, so PCSX2 stops deinterlacing it - which otherwise softens every line under the Blend modes and shimmers under Bob. Leaves the boot-menu 480p mode alone.
gsinterlacemode=1
patch=1,EE,001bb0f4,word,24020002
patch=1,EE,003984d0,word,0000001d

[Remove Blur]
author=heavyjam
description=Removes the full-screen flicker filter. On its way to the display buffer every finished frame is composited three times - the line itself, the line above at 50 percent and the line below at 33 percent - which leaves each output line an even average of three source lines. It was built to tame interlace flicker on a CRT; on a progressive display it is a pure vertical smear across edges, the HUD and text, and with No-Interlacing there is no flicker left for it to hide. Vertical detail measures about 30 percent higher with it off, horizontal is untouched, and because the three weights sum to one the image brightness does not change - nothing needs compensating afterwards.
patch=1,EE,001b9988,word,24070000
patch=1,EE,001b99b8,word,24070000
